# Hybrid

Inner layers stay horizontal and shared. The outer edge is vertical. Two features must not each grow a private copy of the same entity.

## Serverpod

```
lib/src/domain/notes/
lib/src/application/notes/
lib/src/infra/notes/
lib/src/presentation/notes/     endpoint and its wire mapper
lib/src/app/
```

The endpoint and its wire mapper both live in `presentation/<feature>/`. Do not add a shared `presentation/mappers/` file. Domain, application, and infra stay one directory each.

## Flutter

```
lib/domain/notes/
lib/application/notes/
lib/data/notes/
lib/presentation/features/notes/     page and notifier
lib/presentation/router/
lib/ui/                              no Riverpod
lib/app/providers.dart
```

`ui/` is presentational. A tile takes values and callbacks. It does not import Riverpod, a repository, or a use case. Feature-only widgets that are not reused stay under `presentation/features/<name>/`.

## Rules

- Use cases stay in `application/<feature>/`. `presentation/<feature>/save_note_use_case.dart` couples the workflow to the screen or the endpoint.
- The composition root stays one place. A new screen adds a feature folder. It does not add a new top-level layer.
- The notifier imports use-case providers from `app/`. The page watches the screen provider. Neither imports `*RepositoryImpl`.
